/**
 * @page data_logging Logging information
 * 
 * @if DOX_NAV
 * @ref guide_book_top "Go back to the guide book topics page"
 * @endif
 * 
 * @section lib_logger Library log handler
 * 
 * By default the library uses a simple log handler, which outputs the logged message to the command line/terminal window. If a library function execution fails, appropriate log level message
 * is sent to the log handler for output to the command line/terminal window. If the terminal window supports colored font, warnings are diplayed in a yellow font, errors in a red font and any
 * other log messages in plain white font.
 * 
 * @subsection lib_log_funcs Logging functions
 * 
 * Information logging functions are not exclusive only to the library functions. API list provides a full @ref logging "list of logging functions" that can be used in the user program to log 
 * important information using the same library log handler if necessary.
 * 
 * The logging functions support the following @ref lime::LogLevel "log levels":
 * <ul>
 *    <li>Critical</li>
 *    <li>Error</li>
 *    <li>Warning</li>
 *    <li>Info</li>
 *    <li>Verbose</li>
 *    <li>Debug</li>
 * </ul>
 * 
 * Logging functions are overloaded and support both the C style formatted string (use of format specifiers. In eg. ``"%.8f"`` and etc.) messages and C++ style string messages. 
 * 
 * @section custom_logger Custom log handler
 * 
 * If the default library log handler is not sufficient, a custom log handler function can be defined and can be used to override the default log handler and its behaviour. Since library logging 
 * functions support both C style formated strings and C++ style string messages, it is possible to define and override both C and C++ style string log handler functions. To override the C style 
 * string log handler, use @ref lime::registerLogHandler(const lime::LogHandlerCString) "registerLogHandler(const LogHandlerCString handler)" function, where the argument is the address of the new 
 * log handler function for C style strings. To override the C++ style string log handler, use @ref lime::registerLogHandler(const lime::LogHandler) "registerLogHandler(const LogHandler handler)"
 * function, where the argument is the address of the new log handler function for C++ style strings.
 * 
 * 
 */